This fixture exercises phpc's deterministic `mysqli_poll()` async-readiness
boundary through a WordPress-shaped `wpdb` connection method. System PHP needs
real async mysqli socket state and by-reference read/error/reject array
mutation; phpc exposes `mysqli_poll()` and `MYSQLI_ASYNC` metadata but rejects
the reached poll because socket readiness, pending async result queues, and
host query execution are not modeled.
